      </div>
      <div>
        <label>&nbsp;</label>
        <button id="stopBtn">Stop</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="small">
      Run the same stream and same variant on two or more browsers. Keep the
      browser sessions alive long enough for tracker discovery and ICE retries
      to become visible. Export the JSON from each browser. In P2P-only mode,
      a stalled/black video with zero P2P bytes is the correct, informative
      negative outcome, not a bug — the stall-rescue timeout exists only so a
      real test session can recover instead of hanging forever; a rescue
      firing is logged and reported as its own distinct event, not hidden.
    </p>
  </section>

